      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:7:4:32:2",
      "text": [
        " قَضَى أَمِيرُ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ ( عليه السلام ) فِي رَجُلٍ ضَرَبَ رَجُلًا بِعَصاً فَذَهَبَ سَمْعُهُ وَ بَصَرُهُ وَ لِسَانُهُ وَ عَقْلُهُ وَ فَرْجُهُ وَ انْقَطَعَ جِمَاعُهُ وَ هُوَ حَيٌّ بِسِتِّ دِيَاتٍ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Muhammad Bin Khalid Al Barqy, from Hammad Bin Isa, from Ibrahim Bin Umar, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘Amir Al-Momineen<sup>asws</sup> judged regarding a man who struck a man with a stick, so his hearing, and his vision, and his tongue, and his intellect, and his private parts ceased to function and his (ability) to copulate went, but he was alive - (a judgement of) six wergilds’."
        ]
      }
    },
